Subject: [PATCH 09/22] tei-v7 struct-09: Forced causal diagnosis before file
 ranking

---
 reranker/reranker.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/reranker/reranker.py b/reranker/reranker.py
index df7b62c..f02039d 100644
--- a/reranker/reranker.py
+++ b/reranker/reranker.py
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@ Map each issue symptom to concrete repository evidence before selecting files. I
 
 Instructions:
 1. Analysis:
-- Analyze the issue and every candidate file using named classes, functions, imported symbols, callers/callees, nearby tests, and graph paths. For every selected file, cite the exact symbol or edge connecting it to the reported symptom, distinguish direct ownership from textual mention, and score evidence strength before ranking files. Prefer files that own the failing behavior or its regression tests over files that merely mention the issue terminology.
+- First write a compact causal hypothesis: observed symptom -> triggering state or input -> responsible function or class -> incorrect behavior -> intended behavior. Then test that hypothesis against every candidate file using named classes, functions, imported symbols, callers/callees, and nearby tests. using named classes, functions, imported symbols, callers/callees, nearby tests, and graph paths. For every selected file, cite the exact symbol or edge connecting it to the reported symptom, distinguish direct ownership from textual mention, and score evidence strength before ranking files. Prefer files that own the failing behavior or its regression tests over files that merely mention the issue terminology.
 - Decompose the issue into separate behavioral clues: public API or user-visible symptom, likely implementation mechanism, callers or configuration paths, and expected regression-test behavior. Track which candidate files cover each clue, penalize rankings that cover only one clue, and note any clues that currently have no repository evidence.
 2. Extraction:
 - Based on your analysis, choose the Top **{}** files and assign each a role: primary implementation, supporting implementation, regression test, or reference-only. Select primary implementation files only when the issue evidence identifies the behavior they own.
